WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.350
Welcome to the Tueri Systems Risk Brief for Sunday, November first.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.208
Operational clarity when conditions change.

3
00:00:07.208 --> 00:00:11.858
A few minutes on what is happening, what can be confirmed, and what has changed.

4
00:00:11.858 --> 00:00:13.349
Digitally narrated.

5
00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:17.764
Two suspected Ebola cases in northeastern Nigeria have tested negative.

6
00:00:17.764 --> 00:00:21.670
Flooding on the Galapagos Islands briefly closed the main airport.

7
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.126
A US Embassy threat alert in Moscow passed without a reported incident.

8
00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:31.976
And a fishing vessel boarding off the Horn of Africa has raised piracy concerns.

9
00:00:31.976 --> 00:00:33.057
Here's the detail.

10
00:00:33.057 --> 00:00:36.130
Nigeria.

11
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:44.861
Confirmed by the Nigeria Centre for Disease Control: two suspected Ebola cases reported in Yola, in Adamawa State, were isolated, and samples tested negative after two rounds of testing.

12
00:00:44.861 --> 00:00:49.308
The center says the case in Abuja remains the country's only confirmed case.

13
00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:52.001
Entry measures are unchanged and not new.

14
00:00:52.001 --> 00:01:00.765
The US Embassy in Abuja says all international arrivals are being screened, and could face quarantine or self-isolation of at least twenty-one days.

15
00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:07.092
The embassy relays that as a Nigerian measure; we have not found Nigerian text on who is quarantined.

16
00:01:07.092 --> 00:01:15.771
Tueri suggests travelers complete Nigeria's health declaration form before departure and allow time for screening on arrival.

17
00:01:15.771 --> 00:01:19.105
Galapagos.

18
00:01:19.105 --> 00:01:28.886
Confirmed by Britain's Foreign Office, updated overnight: the Galapagos regional government declared an emergency after flooding on Santa Cruz island, with road closures, power cuts and disruption to travel to Baltra airport.

19
00:01:28.886 --> 00:01:34.617
The US Embassy advises avoiding the road between Puerto Ayora and the highlands.

20
00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:50.881
Reported, per Ecuadorian officials quoted in local media: Baltra suspended flights for several hours on Saturday and commercial flights resumed that afternoon; one person died and two are missing; about two thousand people are affected; and piped water in Puerto Ayora is suspended.

21
00:01:50.881 --> 00:01:52.903
Some visitor sites are closed.

22
00:01:52.903 --> 00:02:01.623
Tueri suggests confirming flights, transfers and accommodation directly with airlines and tour operators before travel this week.

23
00:02:01.623 --> 00:02:04.095
Moscow.

24
00:02:04.095 --> 00:02:13.894
Confirmed on the US Embassy's website: on Saturday it warned of a credible threat of a mass casualty event at a large museum park in southern Moscow, and advised avoiding the site that day.

25
00:02:13.894 --> 00:02:22.456
Reported, via Russian media: the security service said it was acting on the information, the park was evacuated and closed, and no incident was reported.

26
00:02:22.456 --> 00:02:25.605
Local media report the park reopened on Sunday.

27
00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:31.893
The US advises against all travel to Russia, and that advice is unchanged.

28
00:02:31.893 --> 00:02:34.951
Horn of Africa.

29
00:02:34.951 --> 00:02:43.426
Confirmed by UK Maritime Trade Operations: a large fishing vessel was boarded by unauthorized people on Friday, and authorities are concerned it will be used as a base for a pirate action group.

30
00:02:43.426 --> 00:02:46.701
UKMTO published the warning about a day later.

31
00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:51.059
Its map places the area off the Horn of Africa, in the Indian Ocean.

32
00:02:51.059 --> 00:02:56.946
UKMTO advises vessels to transit with caution and follow best management practices.

33
00:02:56.946 --> 00:02:58.429
Operations check.

34
00:02:58.429 --> 00:03:07.976
Aviation: at about two forty p.m. local time, Flightradar twenty-four showed about a quarter of Riyadh flights cancelled and about four percent at Dammam.

35
00:03:07.976 --> 00:03:12.857
Those snapshots are counted differently from Saturday's, so no trend can be drawn.

36
00:03:12.857 --> 00:03:23.192
Maritime: Iran's Hormuz authority said action against vessels linked to a South Korean shipping group would start today; we found no new statement, so this is a claim only.

37
00:03:23.192 --> 00:03:27.616
Reported: Korean shipowners say the vessels are not owned by that group.

38
00:03:27.616 --> 00:03:34.649
We found no new joint maritime threat update; the last one rates Hormuz severe and the wider Gulf substantial.

39
00:03:34.649 --> 00:03:42.775
Reported: Bulgarian military prosecutors have opened an investigation into last week's drone strike on a container ship off Bulgaria.

40
00:03:42.775 --> 00:03:48.029
Borders and health: the US Ebola attestation rule applies to flights from eleven fifty-nine p.m.

41
00:03:48.029 --> 00:03:50.199
Eastern on Tuesday.

42
00:03:50.199 --> 00:03:51.690
That is unchanged.

43
00:03:51.690 --> 00:04:01.370
Infrastructure, reported: in Andhra Pradesh, officials say thirty-nine of five hundred fifty-two substations hit by Cyclone Arnab were still being restored.

44
00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:08.051
Security: in Honduras, the weekend threat window at Puerto Cortés passed with no incident reported; officials call it a possible false alarm.

45
00:04:08.051 --> 00:04:10.721
We have not seen the US alert lifted.

46
00:04:10.721 --> 00:04:14.469
In the Philippines, Mayon volcano stays at alert level three, reported.

47
00:04:14.469 --> 00:04:24.546
Ground transport: Spain's Madrid to Andalusia high-speed line remains suspended until further notice, according to the rail infrastructure operator.

48
00:04:24.546 --> 00:04:27.147
That's today's brief.

49
00:04:27.147 --> 00:04:28.680
Current as of five forty-five a.m.

50
00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.259
Central, Sunday.

51
00:04:32.259 --> 00:04:34.704
Tueri summarizes public reporting.

52
00:04:34.704 --> 00:04:39.233
It is not legal, medical, or security advice for any specific situation.

53
00:04:39.233 --> 00:04:41.608
Check the original source before you act.

54
00:04:41.608 --> 00:04:50.464
Tueri Systems provides information verification, communications support, and operational decision support for organizations working in changing conditions.

55
00:04:50.464 --> 00:04:53.083
Learn more at tuerisystems.com.

56
00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:54.193
Thanks for listening.
